  m_Name: Solar System
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DataSet
  english: "In the vast darkness of space, at the center of our cosmic neighborhood,
    burns the Sun \u2014 a\r\ncolossal star with a radius of 696,340 kilometers and
    a mass of 1.989 \xD7 10\xB3\u2070 kilograms.\r\nIt is the source of light, heat,
    and gravity, holding every planet in its eternal embrace.\r\nClosest to the Sun
    is Mercury.\r\nWith a radius of 2,440 kilometers, a mass of 3.3 \xD7 10\xB2\xB3
    kilograms, and an average distance of\r\n57.9 million kilometers from the Sun,
    Mercury is a world of extremes.\r\nScorching days and freezing nights shape this
    rocky planet, scarred by ancient craters.\r\nNext comes Venus, nearly Earth\u2019s
    twin in size.\r\nIt has a radius of 6,052 kilometers, a mass of 4.87 \xD7 10\xB2\u2074
    kilograms, and orbits 108 million\r\nkilometers from the Sun.\r\nIts thick, toxic
    atmosphere traps heat, making Venus the hottest planet in our solar system.\r\nOur
    home, Earth, lies 149.6 million kilometers from the Sun.\r\nWith a radius of
    6,371 kilometers and a mass of 5.97 \xD7 10\xB2\u2074 kilograms, it is the only
    known\r\nplanet to support life.\r\nLiquid water, a protective atmosphere, and
    perfect balance make Earth truly unique.\r\nBeyond Earth is Mars, the Red Planet.\r\nMars
    has a radius of 3,390 kilometers, a mass of 6.42 \xD7 10\xB2\xB3 kilograms, and
    orbits 227.9 million\r\nkilometers from the Sun.\r\nOnce rich with water, Mars
    now stands cold and dusty, yet full of mystery.\r\nFarther out lies Jupiter,
    the giant of the solar system.\r\nWith a massive radius of 69,911 kilometers,
    a mass of 1.9 \xD7 10\xB2\u2077 kilograms, and a distance of\r\n778 million kilometers,
    Jupiter dominates with gravity.\r\nIts swirling storms and Great Red Spot reveal
    a world of endless turbulence.\r\nSurrounded by dazzling rings is Saturn.\r\nIt
    has a radius of 58,232 kilometers, a mass of 5.68 \xD7 10\xB2\u2076 kilograms,
    and orbits 1.43 billion\r\nkilometers from the Sun.\r\nSaturn\u2019s beauty hides
    violent winds and crushing pressure beneath its clouds.\r\nBeyond Saturn drifts
    Uranus, tilted on its side.\r\nWith a radius of 25,362 kilometers, a mass of
    8.68 \xD7 10\xB2\u2075 kilograms, and a distance of 2.87\r\nbillion kilometers,
    it rotates unlike any other planet.\r\nIts icy atmosphere glows faintly blue
    under distant sunlight.\r\nAt the edge of the solar system lies Neptune.\r\nIt
    has a radius of 24,622 kilometers, a mass of 1.02 \xD7 10\xB2\u2076 kilograms,
    and orbits 4.5 billion\r\nkilometers from the Sun.\r\n\r\nHere, supersonic winds
    rage across a frozen, mysterious world.\r\nTogether, these planets form our solar
    system \u2014 a delicate dance of gravity, time, and cosmic\r\nwonder."
  hindi: "\u0905\u0902\u0924\u0930\u093F\u0915\u094D\u0937 \u0915\u0947 \u0905\u0938\u0940\u092E
